# Editorial Master Constitution (always on)

Before any novel/prose/timeline/ledger work, obey:

`00_CANON/03_EDITORIAL_MASTER_CONSTITUTION.md`

That file outranks chat improvisation. Read it fully when starting a new novel task or when unsure.

## Non-negotiables (pocket)

1. **Name the mode:** analysis / continuity / calendar / motif / expansion / polish / docs / export.
2. **Identify the current master file** before editing. Do not assume Markdown if DOCX is ahead (or reverse). Reconcile splits first.
3. **Continuity > polish.** Names, kinship, dates, distance, objects, promises beat elegant rewrites.
4. **Human-first.** No institutional lectures; chapters open on human problems.
5. **Do not tidy deferred mysteries** (guest identity, Lakshmi’s unfinished sentence, Gayatri/traveler networks, Book 1 Coda) unless explicitly ordered.
6. **Voice:** restraint, object-anchoring, India as structure — not AI-smoothed “lyrical” or pulp stakes inflation.
7. **Same-session docs:** if prose facts change, update ledgers/timeline/lock notes/CHANGELOG in the same pass.
8. **Analysis-only means no manuscript edits.**
9. Genre contract: **upmarket commercial literary fiction** as defined in the constitution §3.
10. When unsure (register, master, calendar, locked lines): **ask**, do not invent.

## Anti-patterns (instant stop)

Solving mysteries early · turning Meera into a detective · explaining Shankarappa’s network · padding to hit wordcount · changing one countdown without dependents · editing the non-master file · completing unfinished artistic silence “to help.”
